    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11[d]">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 11[d]</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11[d]" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="454" ed="#liebermann"/>[11[d]] ofn ⁊ aste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ger_11-d.lnote.oe.6"/> ⁊ fela ðinga sceal to tune — ge eac henna hrost;</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="26.3" corresp="#wit-b">Ofn . 7 aste . 7 fela ðinga sceal|to tune ge eac henna hrost .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="336" ed="#rabin-doml"/>ofn and aste and fela ðinga sceal to tune, ge eac henna hrost.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="454" ed="#liebermann"/>Ofen und Trockenofen und viele Dinge gehören zum Gutsgehöft — wie auch Hühnersteige;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">an oven and a drying-kiln and many things belong to the estate — and also a hen-roost;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">[To make] an oven and a kiln, and many things must [be done] about the estate, likewise [to make] chicken roosts.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="337" ed="#rabin-doml"/>and do many other things on the estate such as building chicken roosts.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">B's ‘aste’ stands for ‘ast’ (compare Rect 6).</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ger_11-d.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">454</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">für</hi> ast; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Rect. 6<hi rend="italic">ᵉ</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for ast; cf. Rect. 6ᵉ</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
